WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
We'll remember this, as the
last day of the republic.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.820
I always try to help out the law.

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:10.040
We don't really know anything
of the rest of the world.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.940
It was my fault, I take
full responsibility.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:14.587
So, let's have a conversation.

00:00:14.587 --> 00:00:17.087
- What would you like to know?

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.033
Bill Weasley.

00:00:44.312 --> 00:00:47.250
If it's the right filmmaker,
I'm willing to do anything.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.050
I'll do two lines or I'll do
the lead or I'll do something

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.090
which isn't flattering.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.490
Good filmmakers are the reason
that I'm an actor at all.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.920
It's because I love good films.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:58.634
So I think I'm also just
willing to throw myself

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.967
into whatever they need
me to be for their movie.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.370
Caroline, you mustn't let
this business get inside you.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.970
The film is a kind of
a gothic ghost story.

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.060
My character grew up very poor.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.630
Always looked up to the upper classes,

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:17.490
wanted to be from the upper classes.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.680
There must be some alternative.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.650
It was a very long process
actually getting the accent.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.820
I worked with a great dialect coach,

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.200
we kind of invented a new accent for him

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.670
because he was from the working class

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:29.350
and yet he aspires to
be from a higher class,

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.360
and yet he can't lose
the accent completely.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:32.980
I'm concerned about his state of mind.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.320
So we kind of invented that.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.310
We also listened to Philip
Larkin reading his own poems.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:40.900
-I work all day and get
half drunk at night.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.280
- He grew up not wealthy and
yet when he read his poems,

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.050
the accent he had was very
posh and then something weird

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.450
happens when you realize
that somebody has changed

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:51.600
themselves in some way
through their accent.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.358
Who do you think you're talking to?

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:02.920
All remaining systems will
bow to the First Order!

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:06.350
Hux is full on fascist,
English upper class,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.918
rolls his R's sometime and it's very

00:02:07.918 --> 00:02:10.790
aspirational and strong.

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:12.760
Hello Harry, Bill Weasley.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:14.710
I thought I had done a
really good job at my accent

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.890
on "Harry Potter,"
until I turned up on set

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:17.810
and went Australian.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.719
True enough, owe it all to a
werewolf, name of Greyback.

00:02:21.719 --> 00:02:24.480
And I couldn't stop being
Australian for a whole day,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:25.949
my first day in front of everybody.

00:02:25.949 --> 00:02:27.760
So that was the worst thing in the world.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.640
What you wanna do is forget
about it when you're doing it

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.000
and just be able to be the character.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.040
It's not my fault, it's not my fault.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.560
They never really loved me.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:36.393
They always loved him more.

00:02:36.393 --> 00:02:38.148
They were leaving me behind.

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:46.810
I don't know those boys.

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.690
I always try to help out the law.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.460
It's funny, southern
American is definitely easier

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.600
than a more general American
or something from either coast.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:57.100
The southern thing, I don't know I think

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.300
because of the way that the sentences work

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.810
and the up and down of the tonality of it,

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:03.709
you can hear it and you can grab on to it.

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:04.700
It's an accent you can grab onto.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.790
South African or Welsh, like
they're the nightmare ones,

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.430
they're the ones that you
just like wake up sweating

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:11.750
about having to do someday.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.523
We always win.

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.510
I mean, I didn't go to drama
school or anything like that

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.730
so it's my own little
system which has developed,

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.220
but yeah, a lot of
exercises in the mornings

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.690
then I tend to keep the
accent up during the day,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.910
just so it settles into my mouth

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.440
and I'm not doing an accent
when we start doing a scene.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.310
It's nothing like that, war shock.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:35.820
Oftentimes I'll find a poem
that I think suits the character

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:37.970
and that will be my mantra that I go to

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.510
because it puts you in
a good state of mind

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:42.120
and it gets your mouth in shape
for what you're about to do.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.050
So my only function was to be someone

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.540
she could use to escape.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.550
I'll keep it up on set,

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:49.210
but then when they say, "cut"
on the last take of the day,

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.100
I go back to Irish and then I can go home

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.610
and talk to my friends and not
have them hate me. You know?

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.623
So I can try and be myself again.

